s they raised. Do: Name the good point and the shortfall in their own terms. Say that feedback like this is appreciated and that they are welcome to contact support if they want help. Avoid: Defensiveness, promises of improvements, and pretending it was all positive or all negative.", "negative/shipping": "Apologise sincerely for the specific problem, without excuses or blame, and offer a route to get help. Focus: Delivery problem (late, missing, damaged, or wrong item): acknowledge that specific problem. Do not state where the parcel is, why it was late, or what will be sent. Do: Name the exact problem they described. Express regret that their experience fell short. Invite them to contact support so the team can look into it. Avoid: Promising any remedy, explaining causes, defending the company, or asking for private details in public.", "negative/quality": "Apologise sincerely for the specific problem, without excuses or blame, and offer a route to get help. Focus: Quality or defect problem: acknowledge the specific defect or failure. Do not guess the cause or promise a replacement. Do: Name the exact problem they described. Express regret that their experience fell short. Invite them to contact support so the team can look into it. Avoid: Promising any remedy, explaining causes, defending the company, or asking for private details in public.", "negative/support": "Apologise sincerely for the specific problem, without excuses or blame, and offer a route to get help. Focus: Service or returns problem: acknowledge their frustration with the service. Do not say what the policy is or promise a refund. Do: Name the exact problem they described. Express regret that their experience fell short. Invite them to contact support so the team can look into it. Avoid: Promising any remedy, explaining causes, defending the company, or asking for private details in public.", "negative/features": "Apologise sincerely for the specific problem, without excuses or blame, and offer a 